      "id": "bbc-2026-09-07-can-the-chancellor-s-positive-vibes-limit-tax-rises",
      "title": "Can The Chancellor's Positive Vibes Limit Tax Rises?",
      "summary": "Chancellor John Healey aims for ‘vibes boost’ in first major economic speech.",
      "body": "Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food         Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live          Use BBC.com or the new BBC App to listen to BBC podcasts, Radio 4 and the World Service outside the UK.Find out how to listen to other BBC stationsEpisode detailsNews,·07 Sep 2026,·41 minsCan The Chancellor's Positive Vibes Limit Tax Rises?NewscastAvailable for over a yearToday, John Healey delivered his first major speech as chancellor, aiming to boost confidence in the economy with a positive message.\nThe chancellor set out his intentions for growth, investment and more jobs. But midway through, Jaguar Land Rover announced they would be making thousands of job cuts after struggling with competition from China and falling behind in the electric vehicle race.\nEconomics editor Faisal Islam and business editor Simon Jack explain what it means for the country, and they chat through Healey’s new ‘Make Great Britain Growth Britain Again”\nAnd we've had a weekend of anti-migration protests. One involved men in balaclavas in Dover and one with a crowd trying to block the migrant coaches in Portsmouth. UK correspondent Daniel Sandford explains.\nYou can now listen to Newscast on a smart speaker. If you want to listen, just say \"Ask BBC Sounds to play Newscast”. It works on most smart speakers.\nYou can join our Newscast online community here: https://bbc.in/newscastdiscord\nGet in touch with Newscast by emailing newscast@bbc.co.uk or send us a WhatsApp on +44 0330 123 9480.\nNew episodes released every day. If you're in the UK, for more News and Current Affairs podcasts from the BBC, listen on BBC Sounds: https://bbc.in/4guXgXd\nNewscast brings you daily analysis of the latest political news stories from the BBC. The presenter was Adam Fleming. It was made by Jack Maclaren with Anna Harris and Lois Worrow.  The social producer was Gabriel Purcell-Davis. The technical producer was Philip Bull and Holly Smith. The assistant editor is Chris Gray. The senior news editor is Sam Bonham.Programme WebsiteMore episodes",
      "source": "BBC",
