      "summary": "Police say they have arrested two men and two women as part of their investigation.",
      "body": "Residents living in Cheslyn Hay, which has a population of about 7,000 people, were said to have been left shocked by the child's death.Councillor Robert Duncan, of South Staffordshire Council, said the community was devastated and urged residents to \"avoid speculation\".People should \"allow the family and responders the privacy and respect they deserve\", he added.The superintendent of the Cannock Chase Methodist Church Circuit, Rev Samantha Hagerman, said: \"Our thoughts and prayers are with family, friends and emergency services affected by the incident near Cheslyn Hay yesterday.\"Sir Gavin Williamson, MP for Stone, Great Wyrley and Penkridge, described it as \"extremely distressing news\" which had caused a lot of concern in the area.He also called for people not to speculate about what happened and to allow police to carry out their investigations.\"I am extremely grateful to the emergency services and my thoughts are with the child's family at this incredibly upsetting time,\" he said on Facebook.",
