      "id": "techcrunch-2026-09-06-phil-schiller-s-app-store-exit-reportedly-driven-by-wariness",
      "title": "Phil Schiller’s App Store exit reportedly driven by wariness over future plans",
      "summary": "Schiller reportedly had reservations about new CEO John Ternus' goal of bringing in more recurring revenue from the App Store.",
      "body": "Why is longtime Apple executive Phil Schiller stepping down from his role as the head of the App Store?\nBloomberg’s Mark Gurman reports that Schiller’s decision — he will remain involved in the company as an Apple fellow working on unspecified projects — was driven in part by a desire to spend more time with his family and on philanthropy.\nBut apparently there was another factor in Schiller’s thinking: New CEO John Ternus and services chief Eddy Cue seek to improve App Store margins and bring in more recurring revenue.\nOf course, Apple’s management of the App Store, as well as its share of App Store payments, has been an ongoing source of developer criticism and has even been the subject of major lawsuits.\nIn Gurman’s telling, there wasn’t a big fight over Ternus and Cue’s strategy. But Schiller believed that trying to squeeze more profits from the business would only increase conflict with governments and developers, so he decided to step down and avoid getting involved.",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Anthony Ha",
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-06T21:41:06.000Z",
