      "title": "How Damaging Is Reform's Donations Row?",
      "summary": "Nigel Farage tells Laura he 'wasn't listening' during foreign donor talks.",
      "body": "Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food         Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live          Use BBC.com or the new BBC App to listen to BBC podcasts, Radio 4 and the World Service outside the UK.Find out how to listen to other BBC stationsEpisode detailsNews,·05 Sep 2026,·34 minsHow Damaging Is Reform's Donations Row?NewscastAvailable for over a yearToday, we look at how much damage the Reform donations report will do to the party.\nNigel Farage has said he \"frankly wasn't listening\" during the conversation with his former chief of staff and an undercover reporter discussing what appears to have been a scheme to funnel foreign money to Reform UK.\nThe row has overshadowed the party’s conference in Birmingham, where Laura, Chris, and Joe got together to discuss Farage’s response.\nThey also look at whether cultural issues are partly to blame for controversies for the party to do with money.\nAnd we look at the policies coming from the event.\nYou can now listen to Newscast on a smart speaker. If you want to listen, just say \"Ask BBC Sounds to play Newscast”. It works on most smart speakers.\nYou can join our Newscast online community here: https://bbc.in/newscastdiscord\nGet in touch with Newscast by emailing newscast@bbc.co.uk or send us a WhatsApp on +44 0330 123 9480.\nNew episodes released every day. If you're in the UK, for more News and Current Affairs podcasts from the BBC, listen on BBC Sounds: https://bbc.in/4guXgXd\nNewscast brings you daily analysis of the latest political news stories from the BBC. The presenters were Laura Kuenssberg, Chris Mason and Joe Pike. It was made by Chris Flynn and Jesse Fox. The social producer was Grace Braddock. The technical producer was Jonny Hall. The assistant editor is Chris Gray. The senior news editor is Sam Bonham.Programme WebsiteMore episodes",
