      "id": "bbc-2026-09-04-isak-shines-at-last-but-scherpen-suffers-ipswich-v-liverpool",
      "title": "Isak shines at last but Scherpen suffers - Ipswich v Liverpool player ratings",
      "summary": "How Liverpool and Ipswich Town's players rated following their Premier League match.",
      "body": "Kjell Scherpen: Desperately poor for Alexander Isak's early goal. Weak and meant Ipswich got off to the worst possible start. A couple of decent saves but the damage was done. 4Dara O'Shea: Led from the front as always but Ipswich's defence struggled against the movement of Isak and the creation of Gakpo. He had a hard time. 5Issa Diop: Towering figure always willing to indulge in the physical changes but this was a tough night after those two early Liverpool goals. 6Jacob Greaves: Stern test against the inspired Cody Gakpo, showing the quality he will face in the Premier League. 5Leif Davis: Tested defensively but was always competitive. Lent weight to attacks and had a chance with a far post header. 6Sasa Lukic: Will bring experience to Ipswich Town but on this night Liverpool's midfield was too powerful. 5Exequiel Palacios: Tried to bring some composure to Ipswich Town's game but was fighting a losing battle. 6Abdul Fatawu: Pace but little end product. Energetic but erratic. 5Julio Enciso: Ipswich's main threat. Tireless. Might have done more with the final ball but never gave up even when odds were against him. 7Daizen Maeda: Anonymous. Made no impact at all and no surprise when taken off. 5Emersonn: Battled hard but no luck against Van Dijk and Jacquet. 5Subs:Jack Clarke (on 66 Maeda): Introduced when the game was lost. 5Zian Flemming (on 66, Emersonn): Couple of bustling contributions. 5Kasey McAteer (on 79, Fatawu).Abdoul Outarra (on 78, Palacios).Subs not used: Walton, Furlong, Kipre, Florentino, NunezAlisson: Lucky to get away with misjudging a first-half corner. The occasional anxious moment but no harm done. 6Ronald Araujo: Strong in the air and on the ground on an impressive Premier League debut at right-back. Important interventions by being in the right place at the right time. 7Virgil van Dijk: Usual unruffled self in the face of some frantic Ipswich Town attacking. 7Jeremy Jacquet: Solid alongside Van Dijk. Continues to look a very fine acquisition. 6Milos Kerkez: Occasionally troubled by Fatawu's pace but never in huge difficulties. 6Dominik Szoboszlai: Driving runs from midfield and always willing to test the keeper. Iraola should never use him at right-back. 7Alexis Mac Allister: Still not quite at his best. Too many misplaced passes but never hides or shirks responsibility. 6Florian Wirtz: Busy but occasionally lightweight. As so often, showed subtle touches that hint at good things to come. 6Alexander Isak: The best of Alexander Isak at last. Running behind a defence with pace and clever movement with cool finishes. Finally showed why Liverpool bought him. 8Victor Munoz: Willing and pacy out wide but could have delivered more end product. 6Cody Gakpo: Could have been playing for Manchester City. How glad Liverpool are he wasn't. Two superb passes for Isak's opening goals, Truly outstanding performance. 9Subs:Bradley Barcola (on 64, Munoz): Showed one or two flashes of the lightning pace the £123m signing will bring to Liverpool. 5Ryan Gravenberch (on 64, Isak): Brought on to shut down any potential Ipswich Town revival.Nyoni (on 84, Mac Allister)Lewis Koumas (on 90, Wirtz)Subs not used: Mamardashvili, Frimpong, Tsimikas, Endo, Ngumoha",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
