      "id": "bbc-2026-09-04-farage-unveils-small-boats-deal-with-french-national-rally-p",
      "title": "Farage unveils small boats deal with French National Rally party",
      "summary": "Reform says it would use the Navy to intercept boats and return migrants to France, if the party wins power.",
      "body": "The \"memorandum of understanding\" unveiled at the conference is a political document, but could be developed into a legal agreement between two future governments, if both parties win power.It states: \"The United Kingdom will intercept boats which have launched from French shores and entered British territorial waters and will return the persons on board to France. \"France will ordinarily accept these persons, who will be repatriated to their home country in accordance with the law in force in France concerning expulsion.\"Challenged during a news conference over whether the wording \"ordinarily\" meant some migrants would not be accepted by France, Farage said it was \"legalese\".He argued the proposals would mean there was \"no incentive\" to pay a trafficker to cross the Channel, and \"in very, very short order the business model is broken\".Farage said the \"historic document\" would \"stop the boats forever\".Achieving this goal within the first 100 days of a Reform government is one of the party's key pledges.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
